        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(security): report browser audit summary from plugin policy",
        "body": "Related: #86138, #76631, #96397, #92086, #92883\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where `openclaw security audit` could report `browser control: enabled` in the attack-surface summary when a restrictive plugin policy excluded or denied the bundled browser plugin and no browser config was present.\n\nThat output is confusing for hardened deployments because the summary line contradicts the effective plugin policy operators use to reduce agent/browser attack surface.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe attack-surface summary now derives the browser-control line from the effective browser/plugin policy instead of treating missing `browser` config as enabled. It keeps current startup-intent behavior: explicit `browser` config still reports enabled, while `plugins.deny`, `plugins.entries.browser.enabled=false`, `browser.enabled=false`, and `plugins.enabled=false` report disabled.\n\nThis is intentionally a narrow audit-output fix. It does not change plugin loading, browser startup, tool exposure, Security Matrix semantics, or agent runtime behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators using `plugins.allow`/`plugins.deny` as a hardening control get a more accurate attack-surface summary. A read-only or minimal deployment that excludes browser no longer sees the summary claim browser control is enabled solely because of config defaults.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused tests:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/security/audit-summary.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       6 passed (6)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/security/audit-extra.sync.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       14 passed (14)\n```\n\nLint/format checks:\n\n```text\npnpm exec oxfmt --check src/security/audit-extra.summary.ts src/security/audit-summary.test.ts\nAll matched files use the correct format.\n\nnode scripts/run-oxlint.mjs --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.core.json src/security/audit-extra.summary.ts src/security/audit-summary.test.ts\ngit diff --check -- src/security/audit-extra.summary.ts src/security/audit-summary.test.ts\n```\n\nPatched collector proof for the hardened shape:\n\n```text\nsummary.attack_surface\ngroups: open=0, allowlist=0\ntools.elevated: enabled\nhooks.webhooks: disabled\nhooks.internal: disabled\nbrowser control: disabled\ntrust model: personal assistant (one trusted operator boundary), not hostile multi-tenant on one shared gateway\n```\n\nRelated-work boundary:\n\n- #86138 owns agent-facing `plugins.bundledDiscovery` hardening.\n- #96397 owns startup warnings for configured channel plugins that cannot load.\n- #92086 owns the broader observe-only Security Matrix runtime-fact model.\n- #92883 is the closest merged precedent: a narrow security-audit predicate fix with focused regression coverage.\n\nThis PR only fixes the browser-control line in `summary.attack_surface`.\n",
        "branch": "fix/security-audit-browser-summary-policy",
